# A&D Billiards site

Static Astro 7 marketing site for a local pool table moving and repair business in North Olmsted, OH. There's no framework UI library and no client-side JS beyond what HTML/CSS can do.

## Where things live
- Content and business facts: `src/data/site.ts` and `src/data/faqs.ts`. Change copy there before touching markup.
- Shared design tokens and utility classes: `src/styles/global.css` (`.wrap`, `.section`, `.band`, `.h1/.h2/.h3`, `.btn`, `.ruled`, `.steps`, `.panel`).
- Page-specific styles go in a scoped `<style>` block in that page or component.

## Design rules
- Palette: felt green `--felt`, walnut `--walnut`, brass `--brass` (on dark green only), cream `--cream`. Don't add new accent colors.
- Type: Archivo Variable for display (often `font-stretch: 112%`, weights 700–900), Source Serif 4 for body.
- Avoid generic "AI template" patterns: no gradient washes, no rounded icon cards, no emoji, no pill buttons. Prefer ruled lists, price-board rows, numbered steps and real photos. Border radius stays at `--radius` (3px).
- Images: put files in `src/assets/photos/` and render them with `astro:assets` `<Image>` (always meaningful `alt`, or `alt=""` for decorative).
- Accessibility: real links and buttons, labels on inputs, 44px minimum touch targets, text contrast at least 4.5:1.

## Content rules
- Never invent facts about the business (prices, years, guarantees, reviews, insurance). Unknowns use `<Todo>…</Todo>` in markup, `null` prices, or `[bracketed]` text in data strings.
- Each page needs a unique `title` and `description` passed to `Base`.
- City pages (`/service-area/[city]`) only exist for cities with a real, specific `intro`. Don't mass-generate templated city copy.

## Commands
`npm run dev`, `npm run build`, `npm run check`, `npm run todos`. Node 22.23.4+.
